data
  title Ping rate: freshness vs write cost
  desc 10M sharers — the interval sets the write firehose
  compares
    - label Ping every 1s
      children
        - label ~10M writes/sec
          desc 10M sharers pinging once a second floods the ingest path
        - label Quadruples write load
          desc vs every-5s, for only marginal extra freshness
        - label Feels live, costs the most
          desc Pays the full firehose even while users sit still
    - label Ping every 5s
      children
        - label 2M writes/sec
          desc 10^7 / 5 — the design's baseline ingest rate
        - label Adaptive when stationary
          desc Slow when still, fast when moving — most realtime feel
        - label A dropped ping self-heals
          desc Next ping replaces it in seconds; no durability needed
